          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सार्थः — sārthaḥ — \"a caravan\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सार्थः ग्रामात् ग्रामं गच्छति। sārthaḥ grāmāt grāmaṃ gacchati. The caravan goes from village to village."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A masculine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सार्थः (sārthaḥ) is built from sa, \"with\", and artha, \"an aim, business\": MW gives sārtha first as having a purpose, then as a travelling company of traders or pilgrims, a caravan (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
